industry":"Drug Manufacturers - Specialty & Generic","summary":"Amylyx Pharmaceuticals, Inc., a clinical-stage pharmaceutical company, engages in the discovery and development of treatment options for neurodegenerative diseases and endocrine conditions in the United States. It provides Avexitide, an investigational, first-in-class glucagon-like peptide-1, or GLP-1 receptor antagonist, which is in phase 3 clinical trial to treat post-bariatric hypoglycemia and congenital hyperinsulinism. The company also develops AMX0035, an oral, fixed-dose combination of sodium phenylbutyrate and taurursodiol which is phase 2 clinical trial for the treatment of wolfram syndrome, as well as in phase 2b/3 clinical trial to treat progressive supranuclear palsy; AMX0114, which is in phase 1 clinical trial for the treatment of amyotrophic lateral sclerosis; and long-acting GLP-1 receptor antagonist to treat post-bariatric hypoglycemia and other rare diseases. Further, it develops AMX0318, a GLP-1 receptor antagonist for the treatment of post-bariatric hypoglycemia and other rare diseaees. Amylyx Pharmaceuticals, Inc. was founded in 2013 and is headquartered in Cambridge, Massachusetts.","employees":136,"website":"https://amylyx.com","country":"United States","city":"Cambridge","officers":[{"name":"Mr. Joshua B. Cohen","title":"Co-Founder, Co-CEO & Director"},{"name":"Mr. Justin B. Klee","title":"Co-CEO & Director"},{"name":"Mr. James M. Frates M.B.A.","title":"Chief Financial Officer"}]},"sector_medians":{"fpe":19.17,"tpe":29.98,"ps":4.488,"pfcf":28.95,"peg":1.365,"pb":4.556,"ev_ebitda":16.93,"rev_growth":0.1,"eps_growth":0.1735,"eps_growth_fwd":0.09465,"eps_growth_next":0.1197,"div_yield":0,"roe":0.01872,"roa":0.02349,"de":41.94,"gross_margin":0.4961,"op_margin":0.03472,"profit_margin":0,"current_ratio":3.1},"valuation":[{"k":"fpe","label":"Forward P/E","v":-1,"sector":19.17,"verdict":"Loss-making"},{"k":"tpe","label":"TTM P/E","v":-1,"sector":29.98,"verdict":"Loss-making"},{"k":"ps","